 "title": "Valid Parentheses",
 "slug": "valid-parentheses",
 "category": "stack",
 "difficulty": "Easy",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-parentheses/",
 "pattern": "Stack of unclosed brackets",
 "statement": "Given a string made only of the characters `( ) [ ] { }`, decide whether it is valid: every opening bracket must be closed by the **same type** of bracket, and brackets must be closed in the correct order.",
 "example": {
  "input": "s = \"([]{})\"",
  "output": "True",
  "why": "Every bracket is closed by its own kind, innermost first."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "s = \"()[]{}\"",
   "output": "True"
  },
  {
   "input": "s = \"(]\"",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "s = \"([\"",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "s = \"]\"",
   "output": "False"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "The bracket opened **last** must be the one closed **first**. That is exactly how a stack behaves: last in, first out.",
  "See an opening bracket → push it. It waits on the stack for its partner.",
  "See a closing bracket → it must match the **top** of the stack. If it does, pop. If it does not (or the stack is empty), the string is invalid.",
  "At the end the stack must be empty — anything left was never closed."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def isValid(self, s: str) -> bool:\n        stack = []\n        parentheses_map = {\")\": \"(\", \"}\": \"{\", \"]\": \"[\"}\n\n        for char in s:\n            if char in parentheses_map.values():\n                stack.append(char)\n            elif char in parentheses_map:\n                if not stack or stack[-1] != parentheses_map[char]:\n                    return False\n                stack.pop()\n            else:\n                return False\n\n        return not stack",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n)",
  "timeWhy": "Each character is pushed and popped at most once.",
  "space": "O(n)",
  "spaceWhy": "A string of only opening brackets puts every character on the stack."
 },
 "steps": [
